    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into high-xwOBA assets and favorable matchups against soft-tossing rotations. **Corbin Carroll** (82.69) and **James Wood** (78.42) anchor our offensive ceiling, both benefiting from ideal leadoff or high-order positioning and matchups against vulnerable pitching. **Corbin Carroll** specifically carries a boosted efficiency score due to a slow opposing battery, creating a prime environment for his elite stolen base potential. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (70.71) serves as our most reliable infield anchor, with his platoon advantage against Young fueling a high projection that transcends the league's standard efficiency floors. We are also capitalizing on **Mickey Moniak** (64.11), whose elevated score is bolstered by a massive +14% park factor, offsetting the challenging xERA of Greene.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Austin Riley** (44.86) on the bench in favor of **Dalton Rushing** (41.40). While **Austin Riley** offers higher raw power, his matchup against Eovaldi presents a significant hurdle that drags his efficiency below the optimizer\u2019s threshold; **Dalton Rushing**, despite the low batting order, maintains a stronger platoon advantage and BvP profile that kept him narrowly in the starting nine. Meanwhile, **Henry Bolte** (48.02) and **Alex Freeland** (46.74) occupy the bottom tier of our starters; both are essentially \"start-to-fill\" choices. We are monitoring **Alex Freeland** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates a quick pivot if his position changes, while **Seiya Suzuki** (62.45) carries a notable warning\u2014his score is dampened by a negative wind factor, though his stolen base upside against a slower pitcher keeps him firmly in the green.",
